    "created_at": "2024-08-05T08:17:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-05T08:35:48Z",
    "body": "Looks like a Safari *issue*. They apparently don't respect `color-scheme: dark light` from inside an `<img>`, nor do they support `prefers-color-scheme` there btw. Maybe for privacy reasons? \r\nThey do however support it when in an `<iframe>` or `<object>`, so it might be a workaround. \r\n\r\nOther affected sections:\r\n\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#link-type-modulepreload\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#url-state-(type=url)\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-multiple-attribute (x2)\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-list-attribute\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#custom-element-reactions\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#overview-of-the-parsing-model\r\n\r\nAlso the [\"tracking-vector\"](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tracking-vector) image's background should probably be updated for dark-mode, currently only Safari renders a visible finger-print path, thanks to that \"issue\".",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
